jCloudflareDDNS is a secure, lightweight Dynamic DNS client for Cloudflare.
It is a plain Java command-line application that compares configured DNS
records with a host's public IPv4 or IPv6 address and can update records using
least-privilege Cloudflare API Tokens.

Configuration is YAML-based and contains no API Token values. The token is read
from the environment variable named by the configuration. The application
supports multiple profiles, bounded retries, and one-shot sequential or
parallel execution.

This port installs the Java application, its runtime dependencies, sample
configuration files, and an optional rc.d supervisor. The service is disabled
by default, runs as a dedicated unprivileged account, and does not install
credentials.
